# Versana Platform Architecture & Strategy

Versana is the ultimate AI-driven SaaS platform designed to be a co-writer, researcher, and project manager for authors. Unlike standard AI chatbots, it is built on a **Dynamic RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) Architecture**, acting as a permanent "Story Bible" with perfect memory via the **Context Matrix**. 

## Proposed Architecture & Tech Stack

### Frontend & Core
- **Framework**: Next.js (App Router) for robust full-stack capabilities, server components, and API routes.
- **Styling**: Vanilla CSS. The design language is "Scrivener meets Notion" (clean, minimalist, soft off-whites, crisp dark text, refined subtle borders). No neon "AI-glow."
- **Text Editor**: **TipTap / ProseMirror**. Essential for building the "Smart Lore Tags" without lagging the UI. We will build custom Nodes/Marks for entity matching.

### Backend & Databases
- **API Layer**: Next.js Serverless API routes orchestrating the AI logic.
- **Relational Database**: Supabase (PostgreSQL) for user authentication, billing (Stripe Integration), workspace and project metadata, and standard document saving. We will support **Multiple Workspaces** so each writing project can live in isolation with completely siloed data.
- **Vector Database (AI Memory)**: **Supabase pgvector**. This powers the "Context Matrix." Paragraphs and Lore Bible entries are converted into embeddings and stored natively in Supabase for instant retrieval, avoiding the need for a separate third-party vendor like Pinecone.

### AI Models
- **Writing/Reasoning**: Anthropic Claude 3.5 Sonnet (for creative writing, nuance) or OpenAI GPT-4o.
- **Fast Tasks (NER/Keywords)**: GPT-4o-mini or Claude Haiku (to minimize latency on hover-cards and background tagging).
- **Image Generation**: **Nano Banana Pro via Gemini 3.1 Pro** for Chapter Ornamentation, lore thumbnails, and Cover Design.

