## Application Zones

### 1. The Marketing Site
A public-facing funnel designed to convert visitors gracefully and achieve massive organic reach. It must aggressively target both casual "always wanted to write" dreamers and serious professional authors.
- **Landing Page**: A stunning, high-converting entrance. Needs compelling sections emphasizing "Why Versana?" (e.g., "Overcome Writer's Block Forever," "Your Co-Author that Never Sleeps," "From Idea to Published in Record Time"). Soft typography, interactive scrolling visualizations showing how the Context Matrix prevents AI hallucinations.
- **Viral & SEO Engine**: Programmatic SEO generation (e.g., dynamic pages for "How to write a [Genre] novel"). Built-in viral loops emphasizing "Created with Versana" on free-tier exports.
- **Features Page**: Deep breakdown of the Multi-Phase mode, Context Matrix, and Smart Lore Tags. MUST include animated bento grids with motion to visually explain complex AI features simply.
- **Pricing Page**: Clear tier outlines (e.g. Hobbyist, Pro Author, Master). Feature lists should avoid overly technical jargon (e.g. use "Infinite Story Memory" instead of "pgvector storage") to speak directly to writers. Include a dedicated Pricing FAQ section.

### 2. The Admin App
A separate restricted zone (`/admin`) for platform administrators. Needs to be sophisticated and highly actionable.
- **User Insights & Churn Risk**: Monitor active users, subscription states, and flag users at risk of churning based on inactivity.
- **Granular Cost Analytics**: Direct API integration to track LLM and Image generation costs *per user* and *per workspace*. Visualized via interactive charts to calculate profit margins against subscription tiers.

### 3. Subscription Gating System
All AI features, standalone tools, and project phases will be shielded by middleware checking the user's Stripe subscription status.
- **Tier 1 (Free / Hobbyist)**: 
  - Access to Phase 1 & 4 only. Basic writing editor.
  - Strict monthly AI word limits.
  - No vector persistence (Context Matrix is session-only).
  - Versana watermark on all exports and generated assets.
- **Tier 2 (Pro Author)**: 
  - Full access to Phases 1-5 & 7.
  - Persistent Context Matrix memory (Supabase pgvector).
  - Supports up to 3 Active Workspaces (Projects).
  - Unlocks Standalone Market Research and Asset tools.
  - Expanded AI word/token limits per month.
- **Tier 3 (Master)**: 
  - Unlimited Workspaces.
  - Unlocked Phase 6 (Cover Design) and high-tier Nano Banana Pro image generation capabilities.
  - Fully automated Auto-Typesetting pipelines and Hosted Mini-Sites (custom domains).
  - Uncapped or highly elevated API usage pools.

### 4. Core Systems & UX Architecture
- **Workspaces Dashboard**: Top-level UI to manage isolated writing projects, ensuring Lore and Context from one book does not bleed into another.
- **The Context Matrix / Lore Bible Dashboard**: A Wikipedia-style database. Every new character, place, or rule is automatically vectorized and saved to Supabase pgvector within the specific workspace.
- **Smart Lore Tags**: Debounced NER (Named Entity Recognition) matching. Hovering shows a pre-fetched Glassmorphism card.
- **Unified Contextual Right Sidebar**: To prevent dashboard clutter and space inefficiency, the right sidebar consolidates global tools and phase-specific tools:
  - **Upper Half (Global)**: The Context Matrix toggles (to enforce context on generators) and the Proactive AI Phase Assistant. Sections use collapsible accordions.
  - **Lower Half (Phase-Aware)**: A dynamic tool dispatcher that mounts tools ONLY relevant to the `Active Phase`. For example, "Beat-to-Scene" generators only appear in Phase 4, while "Fact Checker" overlays only appear in Phase 3.
- **The Expansion Engine**: Algorithms to deconstruct a short story and inject sub-plots to stretch it into a book, novel, or n-book series.

